{:lesson/id :area-under-curve
 :lesson/title "Area under a curve, and the shell method"
 :lesson/version "1.0.0"
 :lesson/slides
 [{:slide/id :question
   :slide/title "The question"
   :slide/blocks
   [{:block/id :intro :block/kind :prose
     :md "How much area lies between the parabola y = x^2, the x-axis, and the vertical lines x = 0 and x = 1?\n\nThe region is curved on top, so no formula from geometry applies directly. The *definite integral* is the tool that answers exactly this kind of question. We write the area as"}
    {:block/id :integral :block/kind :tex
     :expr (integral (expt x 2) x 0 1)}
    {:block/id :reading :block/kind :prose
     :md "Read it as: integrate f(x) = x^2 with respect to x, from x = 0 to x = 1. The rest of this lesson is about what that symbol *means* (a limit of sums of thin rectangles) and how to *compute* it (an antiderivative)."}]}

